@@ -0,0 +1,41 @@
+# smallpt playground
+
+Kevin Beason’s [smallpt](https://www.kevinbeason.com/smallpt/) path tracer, compiled from C++ to WebAssembly with Emscripten. `index.html` displays its Cornell box and automatically starts a client-side render. **Randomize & render** changes both object-sphere colors and starts a fresh render. Settings control sample count and resolution; the download icon exports the completed canvas as PNG.
+
+## Run
+
+```sh
+npm start
+```
+
+Serve this directory over HTTP; opening `index.html` using `file://` does not support module workers. The compiled `public/smallpt.js` and `public/smallpt.wasm` are included, so Emscripten is not required to run the site. No server rendering, shared memory, special isolation headers, or third-party rendering libraries are used.
+
+## Rebuild
+
+Install Emscripten and put `em++` on PATH, then run:
+
+```sh
+npm run build
+```
+
+`vendor/smallpt.cpp` is the untouched upstream source. `src/smallpt-web.cpp` retains the original scene and radiance algorithm, replaces the file-writing main function with a small RGBA-buffer API, and adds controllable sphere colors and random seeds. The build emits an optimized, modular ES module with assertions enabled and a growing heap. The renderer runs in `public/render-worker.js`; four-row batches update the canvas and progress. Starting a new render terminates the previous worker.
+
+## Verification
+
+```sh
+npm test
+```
+
+The test runs the actual browser ES module in a worker-like Node VM realm and executes its Wasm. It checks initialization, varied opaque RGBA output, identical output across row-batch sizes, changed output for changed sphere colors, and rejection of invalid dimensions. No manual browser verification is performed.
+
+The initial preview is also generated from the same compiled Wasm, at 640 × 480 and 128 samples per pixel:
+
+```sh
+node --experimental-vm-modules scripts/preview.mjs
+```
+
+The UI uses Google Fonts with system-font fallbacks. It does not need stock photos or generated imagery: every scene pixel comes from smallpt.
+
+## License
+
+smallpt is Copyright © 2006–2008 Kevin Beason, distributed under the MIT license. See `vendor/LICENSE.txt`.
